# Special functions

Gamma and Beta, the error function, Lambert's $W$, Bessel functions, the orthogonal polynomials and complete elliptic integrals. All are built in, under their textbook names when applied: $\Gamma(z)$, $B(a, b)$, $W(x)$, $W_{-1}(x)$, $J_n(x)$, $P_n(x)$, $T_n(x)$, $U_n(x)$, $K(k)$, $E(k)$, and `\operatorname{erf}`. Exact arguments give exact answers where a closed form exists; otherwise the answer is a decimal. Import with `![[std/special.mpp]]`.

## Gamma and Beta

$\Gamma(z) = \int_0^\infty t^{z-1} e^{-t}\,dt$ for $\operatorname{Re} z > 0$, with $\Gamma(1/2) = \sqrt{\pi}$ and $\Gamma(n + 1) = n!$ for whole numbers $n \ge 0$.

$$ \Gamma\left(\frac{1}{2}\right) \overset{?}{=} \sqrt{\pi} $$

$$ \Gamma(6) \overset{?}{=} 5! $$

$$ \int_0^{\infty} t^{2} e^{-t} \, dt \overset{?}{=} \Gamma(3) $$

$$ \Gamma\left(\frac{3}{2}\right) \overset{?}{=} \frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2} $$

$B(a, b) = \Gamma(a)\Gamma(b)/\Gamma(a + b)$ for $a, b > 0$.

$$ B(2, 3) \overset{?}{=} \frac{\Gamma(2) \Gamma(3)}{\Gamma(5)} $$

$$ B(\tfrac{1}{2}, \tfrac{1}{2}) \overset{?}{=} \pi $$

$$ \int_0^1 t^2 (1 - t)^3 \, dt \overset{?}{=} B(3, 4) $$

## The error function

$\operatorname{erf}(x) = \frac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}} \int_0^x e^{-t^2}\,dt$, with $\operatorname{erf}(0) = 0$; it tends to 1 for large $x$.

$$ \operatorname{erf}(0) \overset{?}{=} 0 $$

$$ \operatorname{erf}(1) \overset{?}{=} \frac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}} \int_0^1 e^{-t^2} \, dt $$

$$ \left| \operatorname{erf}(\tfrac{1}{2}) - 0.520499877813046537682746653892 \right| < 10^{-29} \overset{?}{=} \text{true} $$

$$ \operatorname{erf}(1) + \operatorname{erfc}(1) \overset{?}{=} 1 $$

## Lambert W

$W(z) e^{W(z)} = z$. The principal branch has $W_0(0) = 0$ and $W_0(e) = 1$; the branch $W_{-1}$ takes the values below $-1$ on $[-1/e, 0)$.

$$ W(1) e^{W(1)} \overset{?}{=} 1 $$

$$ W_0(0) \overset{?}{=} 0 $$

$$ W(e) \overset{?}{=} 1 $$

$$ W_{-1}(-0.1) e^{W_{-1}(-0.1)} \overset{?}{=} -0.1 $$

$$ \left| W(1) - 0.567143290409783872999968662210 \right| < 10^{-29} \overset{?}{=} \text{true} $$

## Bessel functions

$J_0(x) = \sum_{k \ge 0} (-1)^k (x^2/4)^k/(k!)^2$, with $J_0(0) = 1$. Twenty-one terms agree with it to about 55 digits at $x = 1$.

$$ J_0(0) \overset{?}{=} 1 $$

$$ \left| J_0(1) - \sum_{k=0}^{20} \frac{(-1)^k (1/4)^k}{(k!)^2} \right| < 10^{-50} \overset{?}{=} \text{true} $$

$$ \left| J_1(1) - 0.440050585744933515959682203719 \right| < 10^{-29} \overset{?}{=} \text{true} $$

The recurrence $J_{n-1}(x) + J_{n+1}(x) = \frac{2n}{x} J_n(x)$, at $n = 1$, $x = 2$.

$$ J_0(2) + J_2(2) \overset{?}{=} J_1(2) $$

## Orthogonal polynomials

The Legendre polynomials: $P_0(x) = 1$, $P_1(x) = x$, $P_2(x) = (3x^2 - 1)/2$; they are orthogonal on $[-1, 1]$.

$$ P_0(x) \overset{?}{=} 1 $$

$$ P_1(x) \overset{?}{=} x $$

$$ P_2(x) \overset{?}{=} \frac{3x^2 - 1}{2} $$

$$ \int_{-1}^{1} P_1(x) P_2(x) \, dx \overset{?}{=} 0 $$

$$ \int_{-1}^{1} (P_2(x))^2 \, dx \overset{?}{=} \frac{2}{5} $$

The Chebyshev polynomials: $T_n(\cos\theta) = \cos(n\theta)$, so $T_n(1) = 1$.

$$ T_3(\cos t) \overset{?}{=} \cos(3t) $$

$$ T_5(1) \overset{?}{=} 1 $$

$$ T_2(x) \overset{?}{=} 2x^2 - 1 $$

$$ U_2(x) \overset{?}{=} 4x^2 - 1 $$

## Elliptic integrals

The complete elliptic integrals $K(k)$ and $E(k)$ with modulus $k$ (parameter $m = k^2$): $K(0) = E(0) = \pi/2$. The pendulum swinging to $\theta_0$ has period $4\sqrt{L/g}\,K(\sin(\theta_0/2))$.

$$ K(0) \overset{?}{=} \frac{\pi}{2} $$

$$ E(0) \overset{?}{=} \frac{\pi}{2} $$

$$ \left| K(\sin\tfrac{\pi}{12}) - 1.598142002112540 \right| < 10^{-14} \overset{?}{=} \text{true} $$

$$ E(1) \overset{?}{=} 1 $$

Legendre's relation, $E(k)K(k') + E(k')K(k) - K(k)K(k') = \pi/2$ with $k' = \sqrt{1 - k^2}$, at $k = k' = 1/\sqrt{2}$.

$$ 2 E(\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{2}}) K(\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{2}}) - (K(\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{2}}))^2 \overset{?}{=} \frac{\pi}{2} $$
